// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
//! WP-1B.07: the registry-driven property harness (arch §5.2, §20).
//!
//! Random sequences of up to 100 requests run through the document actor's state machine
//! (`DocState`, deterministic ids, frozen clock) by two actors, `user` and `agent:prop`, as
//! implicit single-command transactions or inside their open batches, gestures and proposals.
//! Each request is generated by `cutweave_ops::testing::arb_command_for` from the current
//! document, for **every registered non-`view` entry**, with valid and deliberately invalid
//! params. After every request:
//!
//! 1. `undo(apply(doc)) == doc` for each successful change: its committed patch inverts
//!    exactly, and `edit.undo` (by the same actor, or the inverse history move for `edit.undo`
//!    / `edit.redo` themselves) restores the previous committed document;
//! 2. `redo(undo(apply)) == apply`: `edit.redo` then restores the changed document;
//! 3. a failed request leaves both documents and both revisions unchanged and emits no patch;
//! 4. the live document survives serialize → deserialize (its JSON value after every request;
//!    the `.cutweave` file text, byte-stable, at the end of each sequence);
//! 5. the invariants hold: `Project::validate`, no overlaps on any track, linked groups intact
//!    (`testing::check_invariants`, `testing::check_linked_edit`) and `DocState::verify`; the
//!    live document is checked whenever no gesture or proposal is open (an open one may
//!    transiently collide with newer commits, which it then cannot commit);
//! 6. `doc.patched` events replayed onto a JSON mirror reproduce the live document, after
//!    every request and once more from the initial document at the end (`replay_events`).
//!
//! Starting documents: an empty project, the WP-1B.06 edit fixture (three linked video/audio
//! pairs, a still and a spare track; this absorbs that WP's `edit_props` test) and
//! `cutweave_model::testing::arb_project` documents. Between requests the harness sometimes
//! closes an actor's connection (its transaction rolls back) or lets 31 s pass (an idle gesture
//! expires).
//!
//! **Scope.** Every non-`view` entry is driven, including the queries, `media.import` (against
//! an `ImportCtx` whose sink registers the batch in one transaction on the actor, as the engine
//! will, and whose analyzer queues a fake analysis job per new asset), the `job.*` commands
//! (against a `JobManager` with seeded job IDs; they never touch the document) and all `edit.*`
//! engine commands: transactions, undo/redo, history, locks and checkpoints. Only `view.*` is
//! left out: it edits UI state, never the document (WP-1C.04 tests it).
//!
//! `PROPTEST_CASES` sets the number of sequences (default 256; nightly runs 4096). Failing
//! seeds are persisted to `crates/cutweave-ops/proptest-regressions/registry_props.txt`.

